  "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/289) by Oskar Grunning (Bitbucket: [sQVe](https://bitbucket.org/sQVe), GitHub: [sQVe](https://github.com/sQVe)).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHey 👋,\n\nI wanna start of saying I’m really loving ART, you’ve done an exceptional job with this software ❤️\n\n‌\n\nI’m on a Fujifilm system and I’m often shooting on the DR200 and DR400 setting to help with dynamic range in SOOC JPGs. I’m noting that ART isn’t reading these values, like Lightroom, and DR200 is underexposed by 1 and DR400 by 2.\n\nIs this something that would be possible to automate? The information is available in the metadata of the RAW files. I’m currently opening a RAW file and just upping exposure with 1 or 2, to get a good starting point. This is a bit of a hassle, and annoying when wanting to batch process RAWs.\n\nAll the best!\n",
